        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore: add provider and scheduler runtime evidence",
        "body": "Fixes #101010\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nProvider and scheduler QA commands could report success without directly proving the runtime behavior they represent. Telegram startup lacked leased-token `getMe` evidence, heartbeat active-hours lacked a bounded real scheduler observation, and the OpenTelemetry smoke delegated production to a broader scenario instead of exercising the diagnostics exporter directly.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds three bounded executable proofs using the shared QA evidence writer: Telegram starts the real monitor only with a dedicated leased QA token and otherwise records blocked evidence without credential data; heartbeat runs the real scheduler through active, quiet-hours, and reloaded configuration states; and the OpenTelemetry smoke starts the diagnostics service directly against a contained OTLP receiver. The older child-process OpenTelemetry path is removed rather than retained as a compatibility layer.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMaintainers get contained runtime evidence for Telegram startup, heartbeat active-hours behavior, and exported telemetry. Generic `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` credentials are never consumed by the Telegram proof, and environments without a dedicated leased token produce an explicit blocked result rather than a false pass.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/e2e/qa-lab/runtime/telegram-bot-token-runtime.test.ts test/e2e/qa-lab/runtime/heartbeat-active-hours-runtime.test.ts test/e2e/qa-lab/runtime/qa-otel-smoke.e2e.test.ts` — 32 tests passed at `03114715609c35db25e4e59e0ef7fa0271640819`.\n- Direct heartbeat executable — passed after observing an in-window fire, a quiet-hours skip, and a post-reload fire.\n- Direct Telegram executable — recorded `blocked` with no dedicated leased token; a generic `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` also remains blocked and is not disclosed.\n- Direct OpenTelemetry executable — passed with 5 spans, 6 metrics, 1 OTLP log, 1 trace request, 1 metric request, and 1 log request.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kww4af8ceg2nf05btch8w679` confirmed dedicated Telegram token and credential-broker inputs were absent. Hosted Vitest and direct execution were blocked before startup because delegated sync omitted tracked `extensions/qa-lab/src/mantis/cli.ts`; local exact-head proof above covers the changed surfaces.\n- Fresh branch autoreview returned no accepted or actionable findings.\n",
